  "summary": "A major earthquake centred beneath Sagami Bay struck the Tokyo–Yokohama area just before noon on 1 September 1923. Collapsing buildings and fires that burned for almost two days destroyed hundreds of thousands of houses. A Japanese government report, as compiled by Nippon.com, counts over 105,000 dead or missing; EBSCO gives a higher total.",
